+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spc-001"></a>
+
+The veterinarian directory answers "which specialties does this veterinarian hold". The specialty directory answers the inverse: one page lists every specialty the clinic knows, each by its stored name, with the veterinarians who hold it shown by first name then last name `[REQ-SPC-001]`. The page only reads; it changes nothing, and NG-2 stands unchanged. Every specialty appears on the one page, so there is nothing to page through. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it — the page lists specialties, not the veterinarian roster. The page is reached by its own address and by nothing else: this change adds no navigation entry and no link pointing to it, on the directory page or on any other (confirmed 2026-08-22). That binds this change, not the system in perpetuity — a visible entry point may arrive as a separate request. The page itself carries the same navigation every page carries, so `REQ-SYS-001` holds on it unchanged.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened at its address, then every specialty the clinic knows is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a specialty held by one or more veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each holder is shown under it by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the directory is opened, then all of them are shown on one page with nothing to page through.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the specialty directory, when it is rendered, then it carries navigation to owner search and to the veterinarian directory.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given this change, when it is delivered, then it adds no navigation entry and no link pointing to the specialty directory, on the directory page or on any other.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+2. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty is shown under each of them.
+3. When the clinic knows no specialty at all, the page renders as an empty directory rather than failing.
+4. Specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one, and so are the veterinarians within one specialty.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
